<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Golden Man</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Issyk Golden Man</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Golden Man is the burial of a richly dressed Saka person found in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issyk-kurgan">Issyk kurgan</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almaty">Almaty</a>, Kazakhstan, in 1969–1970. The clothing and tall pointed headdress were covered with about 4,000 gold ornaments in the animal style, and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> bowl in the grave bears a short, still undeciphered inscription. A reconstruction stands on the Independence Monument in Almaty as a national symbol.</p></div>
